A||N||37||pureGSR||don't own one but you guys are making me think otherwise||||1||
Z||000000||pureGSR||11-01-2001||07:13 PM||||Hi,<BR>I crashed my car (import) last week and now I'm looking around for a different project car.  I stumbled across this forum, expecting it to be a typical GM board.  But even just after 5 minutes of browsing and reading through some of the posts, you guys seem very different from the typical Firebird drivers.  You guys are actually open-minded and willing to share your knowledge with each other.  <BR>Well, I don't own a Fiero and I don't really know anything about them besides the fact that they are RWD mid-engine cars.  If anyone can give me an overview or direct me to the right direction, that would be awesome.  <BR>Couple questions I have in mind are:<BR>1) how hard exactly is it to work on the engine?<BR>2) how does it compare to the MR2's?<BR>3) what kind of swap can i do?<BR>4) how well does the car handle and how reliable is it?<BR>Thanks in advance!<BR>~Steve||||reg||1
Z||000001||pureGSR||11-01-2001||07:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pureGSR:<BR><B><BR>2) how does it compare to the MR2's?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I'm reading through some other posts, I think I just opened up a can of worms, didn't I?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sootah||11-01-2001||07:26 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.1fst2m6.com/1fstsun21.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg"> <P>Just pointin' ya in the right direction.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><B><I>-Sootah</B></I><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||12
Z||000003||FieroFanaticus2||11-01-2001||07:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pureGSR:<BR><B>Couple questions I have in mind are:<BR>1) how hard exactly is it to work on the engine?<BR>2) how does it compare to the MR2's?<BR>3) what kind of swap can i do?<BR>4) how well does the car handle and how reliable is it?<BR>Thanks in advance!<BR>~Steve</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1.  Easy!  Everything is pretty much right there in front of you.  If you can't get to it from the top, most likely you can from the bottom.<P>2.  No Idea, never driven an MR2.<P>3.  How's an LT1 350 sound?<P>4.  '87 and '88's handle better than the earlier models, but in any year or model they like to hold the road really good.  Responsive steering around corners.  It's about reliable as any other 80's GM car.  Also depends on how you take care of it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||LT1 Chop Top||11-01-2001||07:39 PM||||Look here...<P>Two different ends of the Fiero spectrum..<BR> <A HREF="http://ucsub.colorado.edu/%7Epattons/Home15.html" TARGET=_blank>http://ucsub.colorado.edu/%7Epattons/Home15.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||11-01-2001||07:39 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.boomtastic.com/images/front1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.boomtastic.com/images/front1.jpg</A> <P>Kinda like this swap <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rick 88||11-01-2001||07:44 PM||||Steve,<P>Welcome to the Forum. First let me say Fieros are an acquired taste. If you get one you will have to put up with ridicule from some less informed car experts. You also have to realize that you will be getting a car at least 13 years old.<P>Every car has things about it that make it difficult to work on. Overall the Fiero is not that bad if you are used to a FWD powertrain already. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I compare the Fiero V6 more to the second gen MR2. Quicker than the base slower than the Turbo. The MR2 is probably the better handler stock but the Fiero especially 88 has a nice ride. There is much more available in performance parts for a stock MR2, but turbo and supercharger(non A/C) are available for the V6. <P>The Fiero is a natural for swaps and offers much more variety than on the MR2.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Reliability is based on how well the car you purchase was taken care of. Other than some idiosyncrasies eg.(headlight motors)common to the Fieros. They are pretty easy to live with.<P>I like the handling of the Fiero over a FWD car. There are also many parts available to improve on this as well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>My recommendation is that you buy the nicest Fiero you can afford and go from there. <P>Good luck on whatever car you decide to replace your GSR with.<P>Rick 88||||reg||7
Z||000007||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-01-2001||07:50 PM||||MR2?  Never wanted to own one.. but I owned my fiero for 10 years.<P>Fieros..in general are pretty easy to repair, (Mid 80's gm parts) <P><BR>Motors? anything from 4 to v8 's will fit. <P>Also motors can be replaced by dropping the suspension and taking it out underneath or from the top<P><BR>Handling?  with the right tires & suspension they handle great.<P>Looks?  They look great stock and have a lot of body mods available from sidescoops to complete car rebodies (Fino,finale,lambo,ferrari)<P>WARNING!!!! these cars are addictive!! Once you buy one, you will want more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Welcome to the forum!<P>||||reg||1
